      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.76,
      "end_seconds": 284.66,
      "duration_seconds": 7.9,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now acute urticaria, possibly allergic is my leading thought, not anything worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.11,
      "end_seconds": 308.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "I think an allergy test makes sense here, for recurrent urticaria"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 309.42,
      "end_seconds": 313.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "I can book that that for Tuesday at 11:30 am"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.77,
      "end_seconds": 322.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "The The treatment will be prednisolone 20 milligrams once a day for three days. It's for hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.22,
      "end_seconds": 325.2,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "mm alright"
    },
